The corresponding 2-spin system (defined on <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> specified with the fixed parameters <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and a variable <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in U</annotation></semantics></math>) is said to satisfy LDC for <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> if for
