<div id="Thmremark3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3</span></span><span id="Thmremark3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Symmetrically, one can define LDC for <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As an illustration, we will focus on the proof of LDC for <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The proofs of LDC for <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> are quite similar.
Below, without other specifications, we use LDC to stand for LDC for <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We first introduce a special form of LDC, called point-to-point LDC and we show it implies LDC.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Point-to-point LDC)<span id="Thmtheorem17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding 2-spin system is said to satisfy <em id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">point-to-point LDC</em> on <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) if for
any <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, any feasible configuration <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> on some <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, and any two vertices <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, the functions
<math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,+}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}(\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,+}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,-}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}(\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,-}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math> are analytic on <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and
their corresponding Taylor series <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}c_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}c_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}=c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}=c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 18</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If a 2-spin system satisfies point-to-point LDC, then it also satisfies LDC.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">When point-to-point LDC holds, we prove LDC by induction on <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=0,</annotation></semantics></math> the assertion holds immediately. Suppose now that the assertion holds when <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math> then when <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\in\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\},</annotation></semantics></math> by point-to-point LDC, the functions
<math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> are analytic on <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and
their corresponding Taylor series <math id="S3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1</annotation></semantics></math>; similar equality holds for <math id="S3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}=\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}},\tau^{\prime}=\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}=\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}},\tau^{\prime}=\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math> (recall that <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math> means the restriction of <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\notin\Lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\notin\Lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> then the two partial configurations are the same. ), and then we have <math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime}\}|=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime}\}|=k</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence we can apply the induction hypothesis. Then the conclusion follows since <math id="S3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(v,u)\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,u)\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(v,\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime})\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime})\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}).</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 19</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of graphs, and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{G}}=\{T_{\rm{SAW}}(G,v)\mid G\in\mathcal{G},v\in V(G)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{G}}=\{T_{\rm{SAW}}(G,v)\mid G\in\mathcal{G},v\in V(G)\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all possible </span>SAW<span id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> trees of graphs in <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and a neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the 2-spin system defined on <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies point-to-point LDC, then the 2-spin system defined on <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> also satisfies point-to-point LDC.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given
a graph <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, a feasible configuration <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> on some <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> which may be empty, and two vertices <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=T_{\rm SAW}(G,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=T_{\rm SAW}(G,v)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of copies of <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 8. ‣ 2.2 Weitz’s algorithm and self-avoiding walk tree ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Strong Spatial Mixing for General 2-Spin Systems:A Unified Approach from Zero-Freeness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>,
we have
<math id="S3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)=P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)=P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)=P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{+}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)=P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{+}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)=P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW},(u)^{-}}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>SAW</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)=P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW},(u)^{-}}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm SAW},(u)^{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm SAW},(u)^{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm SAW},(u)^{-}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm SAW},(u)^{-}}</annotation></semantics></math>) denotes the partial configuration on <math id="S3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by maintaining <math id="S3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm SAW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm SAW}}</annotation></semantics></math> and pinning all free vertices in <math id="S3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S3.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>).
These rational functions are analytic on <math id="S3.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, notice that <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}}},\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}}},\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{-}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{-}}</annotation></semantics></math> only differ on a finite set <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u)</annotation></semantics></math> of vertices in <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{T}(v,{u})\geq d_{G}(v,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{T}(v,{u})\geq d_{G}(v,u)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We may apply the point-to-point LDC property successively to the SAW tree <math id="S3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, and obtain that the Taylor series <math id="S3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}}}}(\lambda)=\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}}}}(\lambda)=\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{+}}}(\lambda)=\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{+}}}(\lambda)=\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{-}}}(\lambda)=\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}c_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>SAW</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{T,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{\rm{SAW}},(u)^{-}}}(\lambda)=\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}c_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}=c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}=c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, <math id="S3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> also satisfy point-to-point LDC.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, it suffices to prove that point-to-point LDC derives from zero-freeness for trees.
We prove this by establishing a Christoffel-Darboux type identity for 2-spin systems on trees.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Before we delve into the general 2-spin system, we first consider a simple case, the hard-core model, the partition function of which is the independence polynomial.
This model is the 2-spin system where <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.</annotation></semantics></math> For the hard-core model, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> proved that LDC holds by using a tool called cluster expansion from statistical physics.
Here, we show that it can also be proved by the following Christoffel-Darboux type identity by Gutman <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.
For a graph <math id="S3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> and a subset <math id="S3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, we use <math id="S3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\backslash U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\backslash U</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the graph obtained from <math id="S3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> by deleting all vertices in <math id="S3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and their adjacent edges (i.e., the subgraph of <math id="S3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the vertex set <math id="S3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash U</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 20</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> be a tree and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> be two distinct vertices in <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for the partition function of the hard-core model on <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{T}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{u,v\}}(\lambda)-Z_{T\setminus\{u\}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{v\}}(\lambda)=-(-\lambda)^{d(u,v)+1}Z_{T\setminus p_{uv}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus N[p_{uv}]}(\lambda)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{T}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{u,v\}}(\lambda)-Z_{T\setminus\{u\}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{v\}}(\lambda)=-(-\lambda)^{d(u,v)+1}Z_{T\setminus p_{uv}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus N[p_{uv}]}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem20.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem20.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique path connecting <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N[p_{uv}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N[p_{uv}]</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of neighbors of points in <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">This identity was extended to general graphs in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> (Theorem 1.3).
By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem19" title="Lemma 19. ‣ 3 Christoffel-Darboux type identity gives LDC ‣ Strong Spatial Mixing for General 2-Spin Systems:A Unified Approach from Zero-Freeness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>,
the identity for trees is already enough for our proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 21</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem21.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the hard-core model defined on a family <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> of trees closed under
taking subgraphs, if the partition function <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-free on a neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it satisfies point-to-point LDC on <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The case <math id="S3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(u,v)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(u,v)=1</annotation></semantics></math> is easy to check. Here, we assume that <math id="S3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(u,v)\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(u,v)\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. For the hard-core model, <math id="S3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{+}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\lambda Z_{G\backslash N[v]}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{+}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\lambda Z_{G\backslash N[v]}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{-}_{G,v}(\lambda)=Z_{G\backslash v}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{-}_{G,v}(\lambda)=Z_{G\backslash v}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{u^{-}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{Z^{-,+}_{G,u,v}(\lambda)}{Z^{-}_{G,u}(\lambda)}=\frac{Z^{+}_{G\backslash\{u\},v}}{Z_{G\backslash\{u\}}}=P_{G\backslash\{u\},v}(\lambda)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{u^{-}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{Z^{-,+}_{G,u,v}(\lambda)}{Z^{-}_{G,u}(\lambda)}=\frac{Z^{+}_{G\backslash\{u\},v}}{Z_{G\backslash\{u\}}}=P_{G\backslash\{u\},v}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{u^{+}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{Z^{+,+}_{G,u,v}(\lambda)}{Z^{+}_{G,u}(\lambda)}=\frac{\lambda Z^{+}_{G\backslash N[u],v}}{\lambda Z_{G\backslash N[u]}}=P_{G\backslash N[u],v}(\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{u^{+}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{Z^{+,+}_{G,u,v}(\lambda)}{Z^{+}_{G,u}(\lambda)}=\frac{\lambda Z^{+}_{G\backslash N[u],v}}{\lambda Z_{G\backslash N[u]}}=P_{G\backslash N[u],v}(\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">In fact, it is easy to see that for any graph <math id="S3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and any feasible partial configuration <math id="S3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> on some <math id="S3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a subgraph <math id="S3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=P_{G^{\prime},v}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=P_{G^{\prime},v}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the family <math id="S3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is closed under taking subgraphs, <math id="S3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, in order to establish point-to-point LDC, it suffices to prove it for a tree <math id="S3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> where no vertices are pinned.
We observe that</span></p>
