</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The following is the celebrated Lee-Yang circle theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem36" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem36.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 36</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem36.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lee-Yang circle theorem)<span id="Thmtheorem36.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem36.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem36.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem36.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1.</annotation></semantics></math>
For any graph <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math>, the partition function <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}(\boldsymbol{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝛌</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}(\boldsymbol{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> of the ferromagnetic Ising model specified by <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and non-uniform external fields <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\lambda}=(\lambda_{v})_{v\in V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛌</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\lambda}=(\lambda_{v})_{v\in V}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero if we have <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{v}|&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{v}|&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{v}|&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{v}|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Note that Lee-Yang circle theorem gives zero-freeness for the partition function of the Ising model regarding the external fields <math id="S5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we need to apply Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem35" title="Theorem 35. ‣ 5 The implication for non-uniform external fields ‣ Strong Spatial Mixing for General 2-Spin Systems:A Unified Approach from Zero-Freeness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>, instead of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem33" title="Theorem 33 (Theorem restated, SSM for 𝛽 in the Ising model). ‣ 4 Zero-freeness implies SSM ‣ Strong Spatial Mixing for General 2-Spin Systems:A Unified Approach from Zero-Freeness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a> which requires zero-freeness regarding the edge activity <math id="S5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span>
            
            
            
          Zeros of the partition function of the Ising model regarding <math id="footnote7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> are known as Fisher zeros <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</span></span></span>.
However, Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem35" title="Theorem 35. ‣ 5 The implication for non-uniform external fields ‣ Strong Spatial Mixing for General 2-Spin Systems:A Unified Approach from Zero-Freeness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a> requires the zero-freeness condition holds for 2-spin systems on graphs even conditioning on some partial configurations.
Thus, Lee-Yang circle theorem cannot be directly adapted to our setting since it holds only for graphs with no pinned vertices.
In order to obtain SSM from zero-freeness,
we first give the following corollary
of Lee-Yang circle theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem37" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem37.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 37</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem37.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem37.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem37.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and integer <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any graph <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> of degree at most <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and any feasible partial configuration <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, the partition function <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\boldsymbol{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝛌</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\boldsymbol{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math>
is nonzero if we have <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{v}|&gt;\beta^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{v}|&gt;\beta^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;|\lambda_{v}|&lt;1/\beta^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;|\lambda_{v}|&lt;1/\beta^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the partition function <math id="S5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{+}_{G,v}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{+}_{G,v}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> of the Ising model with non-uniform external fields on a graph <math id="S5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> with a vertex <math id="S5.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> pinned to <math id="S5.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex33X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z^{+}_{G,v}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda})=\sum_{\sigma:V\backslash\{v\}\rightarrow\{+,-\}}\beta^{m(\sigma)}\lambda_{v}\prod\limits_{w\in V\backslash\{v\}\atop\sigma(w)=+}\lambda_{w}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></mfrac></msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z^{+}_{G,v}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda})=\sum_{\sigma:V\backslash\{v\}\rightarrow\{+,-\}}\beta^{m(\sigma)}\lambda_{v}\prod\limits_{w\in V\backslash\{v\}\atop\sigma(w)=+}\lambda_{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of <math id="S5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(+,+)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(+,+)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-,-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-,-)</annotation></semantics></math> edges in <math id="S5.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> under the configuration <math id="S5.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math> together with <math id="S5.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> pinned to <math id="S5.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of <math id="S5.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(+,+)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(+,+)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-,-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-,-)</annotation></semantics></math> edges in <math id="S5.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\backslash\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\backslash\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math> under the configuration <math id="S5.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="S5.p10.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m(\sigma)=m^{\prime}(\sigma)+|\{w\in N(v)\mid\sigma(w)=+\}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\sigma)=m^{\prime}(\sigma)+|\{w\in N(v)\mid\sigma(w)=+\}|</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of neighbors of <math id="S5.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have</span></p>
