<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the equality by induction on <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=d(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=d(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\cap\Lambda=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\cap\Lambda=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> are adjacent, Denote <math id="A1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v_{1},\cdots,v_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v_{1},\cdots,v_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> neighbors of <math id="A1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v,v_{l+1},\cdots,v_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v,v_{l+1},\cdots,v_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> neighbors of <math id="A1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, as illustrated in the following figure, then</span></p>
