</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\cap\Lambda\neq\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\cap\Lambda\neq\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>, we argue by induction on <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=d_{P}(u,P\cap\Lambda)+d_{P}(v,P\cap\Lambda)\geq 2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=d_{P}(u,P\cap\Lambda)+d_{P}(v,P\cap\Lambda)\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math> The basic case <math id="A1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=2</annotation></semantics></math> is simple and the process of induction is exactly as above.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Comparison with the cluster expansion approach</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>,
the <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">local dependence of coefficients</em> (LDC) property is proved using <em id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cluster expansions</em> for the hard-core model.
We first review the cluster expansion formulation.
Then, we discuss its limitations in extending to general 2-spin systems, and explain why the Christoffel-Darboux type identity introduced in the present paper can circumvent the obstacle.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Review of the cluster expansion approach</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the hard-core model on a graph <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> with fugacity <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, the ratio</p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{\lambda Z_{G\setminus N[v]}(\lambda)}{Z_{G}(\lambda)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{\lambda Z_{G\setminus N[v]}(\lambda)}{Z_{G}(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(which for positive <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> equals the marginal probability that vertex <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is occupied) admits a series expansion around <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> derived from the cluster expansion of the multivariate independence polynomial.
Concretely, viewing <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> as the specialization of the multivariate polynomial
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}(\mathbf{w})=\sum_{I\subseteq V\atop I\text{ indep.}}\prod_{u\in I}w_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> indep.</mtext></mrow></mfrac></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}(\mathbf{w})=\sum_{I\subseteq V\atop I\text{ indep.}}\prod_{u\in I}w_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{u}\equiv\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{u}\equiv\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains near <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}(\lambda)=\sum_{k\geq 1}\frac{1}{k!}\sum_{v_{1},\dots,v_{k}\in V}\phi\bigl(G(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})\bigr)\,m_{v}(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})\,\lambda^{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}(\lambda)=\sum_{k\geq 1}\frac{1}{k!}\sum_{v_{1},\dots,v_{k}\in V}\phi\bigl(G(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})\bigr)\,m_{v}(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})\,\lambda^{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is the cluster induced by the (not necessarily distinct) vertices <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},\dots,v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},\dots,v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Ursell function of a graph <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{v}(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{v}(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> counts the occurrences of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> among <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},\dots,v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},\dots,v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(H)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(H)=0</annotation></semantics></math> unless <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is connected, the coefficient of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.
This immediately yields the LDC property for the hard-core model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For graph homomorphism measures, a similar cluster expansion is obtained by realizing the partition function as the independence polynomial of an auxiliary graph <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> whose vertices correspond to connected subgraphs of the original graph.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> be a graph and let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a symmetric <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\times q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\times q</annotation></semantics></math> matrix.
We consider the partition function with an external field <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in\mathbb{C}^{V\times[q]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in\mathbb{C}^{V\times[q]}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z_{G}(A,\xi)=\sum_{\phi:V\to[q]}\prod_{v\in V}\xi_{v,\phi(v)}\prod_{uv\in E}A_{\phi(u),\phi(v)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}(A,\xi)=\sum_{\phi:V\to[q]}\prod_{v\in V}\xi_{v,\phi(v)}\prod_{uv\in E}A_{\phi(u),\phi(v)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Fix a boundary condition <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma:\Lambda\to[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma:\Lambda\to[q]</annotation></semantics></math> on some <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V\setminus\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V\setminus\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The goal is to expand the ratio</p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v,i;A}^{\sigma}(z)=\frac{Z_{G,v,i}^{\sigma_{v,i}}(J+z(A-J))}{Z_{G}^{\sigma}(J+z(A-J))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v,i;A}^{\sigma}(z)=\frac{Z_{G,v,i}^{\sigma_{v,i}}(J+z(A-J))}{Z_{G}^{\sigma}(J+z(A-J))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">around <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is the all-ones matrix.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Auxiliary graph <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The vertex set of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> consists of all connected subgraphs <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=(S,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=(S,F)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with at least one edge (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>).
Two vertices <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}=(S_{1},F_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}=(S_{1},F_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}=(S_{2},F_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}=(S_{2},F_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> are adjacent in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}\cap S_{2}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}\cap S_{2}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus an independent set in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a collection of pairwise vertex-disjoint connected subgraphs of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weights.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a vertex <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=(S,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=(S,F)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, its weight <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\sigma}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\sigma}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\sigma}(H):=\frac{z^{|F|}\,Z_{H}^{\sigma}(A-J,\xi)}{\Bigl(\prod_{v\in S\setminus\Lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{q}\xi_{v,i}\Bigr)\cdot\prod_{v\in\Lambda\cap S}\xi_{v,\sigma(v)}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\sigma}(H):=\frac{z^{|F|}\,Z_{H}^{\sigma}(A-J,\xi)}{\Bigl(\prod_{v\in S\setminus\Lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{q}\xi_{v,i}\Bigr)\cdot\prod_{v\in\Lambda\cap S}\xi_{v,\sigma(v)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{H}^{\sigma}(A-J,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{H}^{\sigma}(A-J,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the partition function on <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> with edge matrix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A-J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A-J</annotation></semantics></math> and external field <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, under the boundary condition <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\cap S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\cap S</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define also the prefactor</p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\sigma}(\xi):=\Bigl(\prod_{v\in V\setminus\Lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{q}\xi_{v,i}\Bigr)\cdot\prod_{v\in\Lambda}\xi_{v,\sigma(v)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>q</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\sigma}(\xi):=\Bigl(\prod_{v\in V\setminus\Lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{q}\xi_{v,i}\Bigr)\cdot\prod_{v\in\Lambda}\xi_{v,\sigma(v)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Polymer representation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma 8 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> states that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\sigma}(\xi)\,Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})=Z_{G}^{\sigma}(J+z(A-J),\xi)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\sigma}(\xi)\,Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})=Z_{G}^{\sigma}(J+z(A-J),\xi),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> is the multivariate independence polynomial of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated at the weights <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\sigma}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\sigma}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}\subseteq V(\Gamma)\\
\mathcal{I}\text{ independent}\end{subarray}}\;\prod_{H\in\mathcal{I}}w^{\sigma}(H)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> independent</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}\subseteq V(\Gamma)\\
\mathcal{I}\text{ independent}\end{subarray}}\;\prod_{H\in\mathcal{I}}w^{\sigma}(H).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cluster expansion of the ratio.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the formal cluster expansion (7) to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z_{\Gamma}(w^{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> and differentiating with respect to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{v,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{v,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains the following series expansion for the ratio (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, Lemma 9]</cite>):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v,i;A}^{\sigma}(z)=\frac{1}{q}+\sum_{\ell\geq 1}z^{\ell}\sum_{k\geq 1}\frac{1}{k!}\sum_{(H_{1},\dots,H_{k})\in\mathcal{C}_{v,\ell,k}(G)}\phi\bigl(\Gamma(H_{1},\dots,H_{k})\bigr)\,\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{v,i}}\prod_{j=1}^{k}\widehat{w}^{\sigma}(H_{j})\Big|_{\xi=1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v,i;A}^{\sigma}(z)=\frac{1}{q}+\sum_{\ell\geq 1}z^{\ell}\sum_{k\geq 1}\frac{1}{k!}\sum_{(H_{1},\dots,H_{k})\in\mathcal{C}_{v,\ell,k}(G)}\phi\bigl(\Gamma(H_{1},\dots,H_{k})\bigr)\,\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{v,i}}\prod_{j=1}^{k}\widehat{w}^{\sigma}(H_{j})\Big|_{\xi=1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
